<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?><!--
    What leaves the device when it is backed up or replaced: nothing goes to the cloud, and a direct
    transfer to a new phone carries the library.

    No cloud backup, by decision (2026-10-08, see docs/CRASH_REPORTING.md for the same choice made
    about crash reports). A backup would put the whole database in Google Drive — subscriptions,
    listening history, the queue and every moment the user wrote — and even encrypted with the
    screen lock, its existence, size and timing are Google's to see. android:allowBackup="false"
    already switches cloud backup off; the root exclusion below says so a second time, so that
    turning the attribute back on would not quietly resume it. The cost is real: a phone restored
    from the cloud comes back without the library, so the moments export and the subscription
    export in Settings are what carry it.

    Device-to-device transfer (cable or direct Wi-Fi, Android 12+) is not cloud and stays on;
    allowBackup="false" does not govern it, this file does. The policy there is "restore the
    library, not the bytes", stated as exclusions so that a new Room table or DataStore travels
    without anyone remembering to come back here:
      - databases/megapodcastplayer.db — subscriptions, episodes, listening positions and the queue.
      - files/datastore/megapodcastplayer_preferences.preferences_pb — the user's settings.
    Not listed because the platform already excludes them: cacheDir (Coil's image_cache and OkHttp's
    http cache both live there) and no_backup/.

    There is no backup_rules.xml counterpart: `android:fullBackupContent` applies only to API 30 and
    below, and minSdk is 34.
-->
<data-extraction-rules>
    <cloud-backup>
        <exclude domain="root" path="." />
    </cloud-backup>
    <device-transfer>
        <!--
            The downloaded audio: gigabytes, and re-downloadable from the feed.
        -->
        <exclude domain="file" path="episode_downloads" />
        <!--
            Media3's own index of what is downloaded and cached. It must not travel without the
            audio files above, or the new phone shows episodes as downloaded that are not on disk.
            Media3 rebuilds it from the (empty) cache directory on first use.
        -->
        <exclude domain="database" path="exoplayer_internal.db" />
        <exclude domain="database" path="exoplayer_internal.db-wal" />
        <exclude domain="database" path="exoplayer_internal.db-shm" />
    </device-transfer>
</data-extraction-rules>
